        "content": "<p>adamrk opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997\">PR #14997</a> from <code>adamrk:abk/resource-table-delete</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>delete</code> previously checked <code>is::&lt;Tombstone&gt;()</code> on every deleted entry, even though the <code>Tombstone</code>s are only used for debugging purposes. This added an extra downcast which should be elided in release builds. Overall this produces an improvement of about 4.5% in the <code>p3_http_proxy</code> benchmark.</p>\n<p>Note that the improvements here seem to be a bit sensitive to inlining, so I added some explicit inlining which helped improve the benchmark results. A comparison against main when both use <code>codegen-units=1</code> still shows an improvement in the <code>p3_http_proxy</code> benchmark, so I think the top line 4.5% improvement is coming from a mix of \"real wins\" and better inlining.</p>\n<p>Benchmark results:</p>\n<p>Main (<code>ffff2e2db24a291f02429f123aba1631fa8eea67</code>):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">wasi</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">http</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">p3_http_proxy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">time</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">18.444</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">µ</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">18.465</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">µ</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">18.491</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">µ</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Found</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">5</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">outliers</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">among</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">100</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">measurements</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">5.00</span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">2.00</span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">high</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mild</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mf\">3.00</span><span class=\"o\">%</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">high</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">severe</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">wasi</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">http</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">p3</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">api</span><span class=\"o\">/</span><span class=\"n\">request</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">new</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                        </span><span class=\"n\">time</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\">   </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"mf\">1.4723</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">µ</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">1.4745</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">µ</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mf\">1.4772</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"err\">µ</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"p\">]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Found</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">6</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">outliers</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">among</span><span class=\