    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"thumbs up\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f44d\" role=\"img\" title=\"thumbs up\">:thumbs_up:</span> pchickey submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997#pullrequestreview-5657294954\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Awesome nice job</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635122394,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793040415
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>github-actions[bot] added the label <code>wasmtime:api</code> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997\">PR #14997</a>.</p>",
        "id": 635160456,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793047727
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>adamrk updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997\">PR #14997</a>.</p>",
        "id": 635410876,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793111464
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>adamrk <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997#issuecomment-6444762951\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997\">PR #14997</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>There was a test failing because it mixed deleting with and without tombstones which isn't properly handled with this change (the whole point is that we don't want to check for tombstones when not debugging). So I moved the type parameter to be on <code>ResourceTable</code> itself which means it's no longer possible to mix the two uses within the same table (and modified the test to only use the debug version).</p>\n<p>I also reran the benchmarks to check that we still see the same improvement.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635411787,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793111634
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>adamrk requested <a href=\"https://github.com/pchickey\">pchickey</a> for a review on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997\">PR #14997</a>.</p>",
        "id": 635411834,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793111641
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>alexcrichton <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997#issuecomment-6444831051\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997\">PR #14997</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>FWIW this was originally just intended as a debugging utility and aid, and IIRC the <code>debug: bool</code> parmeter is only there to aid with testing the implementation should the flag ever turn to <code>true</code>. In that sense I don't think it's worth going too far out of our way to keep supporting this -- if it's a perf problem I'd say we could just delete the support outright entirely since it's all off-by-default anyway. Dealing with sealed traits, impls, default type parameters, etc, to me feels a bit heavyweight relative to what it's trying to do.</p>\n<p>Or, alternatively, for the perf problems you were seeing, is that all because <code>debug: bool</code> wasn't inlined to get const-propagated away? If that's the case then <code>#[inline]</code> could help, but I'd again consider keeping a debug-only utility like this a nice-to-have and would prioritize jettisoning it if it's causing problems.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635412809,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793111811
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>alexcrichton <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997#issuecomment-6445120906\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997\">PR #14997</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>(feel free to land this though in the meantime, I'm mostly just musing that as a debug-only feature it's fine to just jettison it)</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635416963,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793112558
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>adamrk <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997#issuecomment-6450197117\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997\">PR #14997</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Makes sense - I'll merge this as is and next time ask if anyone is actually still using the thing...</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Or, alternatively, for the perf problems you were seeing, is that all because debug: bool wasn't inlined to get const-propagated away?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Pure inlining wouldn't have been sufficient before because eliding the check for a <code>Tombstone</code> would require knowing that no <code>Tombstone</code>s exist (i.e. that <code>delete_maybe_debug</code> was _never_ called with <code>debug: true</code>), not just that <code>debug</code> is a <code>const false</code> in the current call. </p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635477429,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793125340
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>adamrk added <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14997\">PR #14997 component: Avoid redundant type check and entry move in <code>ResourceTable::delete</code></a> to the merge queue</p>",
